---
description: Resource models must declare MAIN_TABLE and reference it everywhere
globs: app/code/Aheadworks/**/Model/ResourceModel/**/*.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# ResourceModel `MAIN_TABLE`

Every DB resource model must declare the table name as a constant and use that constant — never hardcode the table string in `_init`, queries, setup references from PHP, etc.

```php
class ShippingClass extends AbstractDb
{
    public const MAIN_TABLE = 'aw_str_shipping_class';

    /**
     * Initialize table and primary key.
     *
     * @return void
     */
    protected function _construct(): void
    {
        $this->_init(self::MAIN_TABLE, ShippingClassInterface::CLASS_ID);
    }
}
```

Elsewhere (collections, joins, raw selects in the same module):

```php
// ✅
->from($resource->getTable(ShippingClass::MAIN_TABLE), …)
// or inside the resource: self::MAIN_TABLE / $this->getMainTable()

// ❌
->from('aw_str_shipping_class', …)
$this->_init('aw_str_shipping_class', 'class_id');
```

Prefer `Api\Data\*Interface` constants for column/PK names; `MAIN_TABLE` is only for the table name.
